<%#
  The engraving — the ledger's hero plate: a corked bottle and a stemmed glass
  standing on a hatched table, lifted from a 19th-century Dutch tavern-sign
  vignette (Rijksmuseum RP-P-OB-30.433, CC0) and traced to vector. Provenance
  and the derivation steps are recorded in docs/ASSETS.md.

  Entirely decorative: the element is aria-hidden, so whatever sits around it
  must carry the meaning on its own. Self-contained — the plate is inline SVG,
  so there is no asset request and no second round trip. It carries no ink of
  its own; `fill="currentColor"` on the root takes the colour from
  .engraving-plate in app/assets/tailwind/application.css (section 12).

  Two things will silently fill the bottle and the glass in solid if this ever
  gets reprocessed, because both destroy the counters — the paper showing
  through inside a stroke, which a trace encodes as subpaths wound against
  their parent:

    - merging the paths (keep svgo's `mergePaths` off), and
    - re-wrapping the `d` data on hyphens, since every `-` here is a sign
      bound to the number after it, not a breakable character.

  Static by design. Nothing here moves, so there is no reduced-motion branch
  to honour.

  Optional locals:
    css - extra classes for the wrapper (e.g. "mt-12" or a width override)
%>
